welcome to another episode on my channel  firm learning  my name is heinrich and as you know on  my channel i want to help you  to become successful in the first years  of your career  here today i'm once again back at my  university of munich  this is the place where i studied  business and philosophy  during my undergrad and the topic of  today's video  is private university versus public  university  private school versus public school and  the question is which  one is better is private university  really  worth the money is it worth the  investment  of your time of your effort and i want  to reflect on this  exactly here at my old university  because indeed  while i did my bachelor in munich in  parallel to that  i completed a semester abroad at bocconi  university in milan  which is a private business school and  then later continued  to do a master in finance and accounting  at the london school of economics  in london so indeed the question is  which one is better  this is what we're going to talk about  today so before we jump into the details  of the pros and cons of public vs  private universities  i first want to specify a bit more what  exactly i mean  by this public university because i know  that here there are significant  differences  also country by country especially also  on the wider regions  so for instance i know that for sure if  in a u.s context  you talk about a public university the  universities that there you would have  in your mind  are probably very different than what  you would talk about in for instance a  german  or broader european context because  indeed here in germany public  universities  like the university of munich are quite  good indeed  and indeed this is a trust similar in  many other european countries as well  so in the context of this video i will  rather talk about this more european  type of system  where while a public university might  not necessarily have the reputation  of some of the very best private ones  they're still considered to be good  and to some extent also competitive and  some of them even target universities  but we're going to talk about this  concept a bit more in a couple of  minutes  i will now talk about four aspects where  private universities potentially a bit  different  than public universities and the first  one is  the richness of experience and this is  now especially relevant when you compare  private  business schools to public big  universities  like for instance the university of  munich and for me one of the key reasons  why i decided to start my undergraduate  studies here in munich  compared to for instance also some  german private business foods that exist  for sure as well  was really the opportunity to study  different  types of subjects different types of  degree programs  and personally i did indeed study  business and philosophy  but even if you are not willing to  complete two full degrees  if you just enrolled in a business  program and then just take individual  lectures individual classes on some  other topics as well  for me this was one of the key parts of  the experience of studying in an  undergraduate degree  and this is of course often not really  possible  in a private business school maybe if  you compare this to the london school of  economics and political sciences which  is the full name of the school  there yes there were some other  opportunities but for instance at my mba  i only had the opportunity to take  business classes  while these were for sure high quality  and very interesting and relevant  business classes  there i missed this opportunity to go  beyond my  core subject same thing was through at  the university bocconi  which is indeed an italian business  school as well and this then also  translates just to the size and  magnitude of university  so here in munich 50 000 students are  studying  this comes with lots of extracurricular  activities  organizations other opportunities that  you could be part of  in parallel to study in university where  things like that exist as well in these  private schools these are often much  smaller  and by that also just the sheer amount  and opportunities of organizations  activities societies  that you can be part of is limited this  is at least what i strongly felt  next point i want to talk about is the  quality of the teaching the quality of  the education  that is being delivered to you and here  i'd assume that many people would argue  that yes the private universities  have an advantage and of course this  might also be the case  especially because due to the better  funding of the private universities  there you will often have smaller group  sizes instead of sitting in a class with  800  900 other students as i often experience  it here at the university of munich  in universities like jealousy where i  studied or bocconi in milan or the later  of course also the mba  the class sizes were significantly  smaller  contributing to a better learning  environment i'd say  and here now right now i'm standing in  front of the business faculty  where i studied here in munich and  indeed it was the case  that why the classes were often larger  especially the later  in the third fourth fifth sixth semester  of university  you had courses you had seminars where  then the group sizes were smaller as  well  so i wouldn't say it's this black and  white when you compare these two types  of universities  though indeed on average i would say it  is correct  that these interactions are richer are  in smaller groups  in the private universities but here i  also want to say that in general the  quality of the lectures the quality of  the teachings  this had not a lower quality munich here  it also had some excellent lectures  excellent classes delivered by excellent  professors  so this i'd say was rather similar  though again  quality of the groups smaller group  sizes this is really  what you get as a pro in this private  context  the next thing i want to talk about are  student fees  and indeed student fees are often one of  the first things that come to your mind  when you talk about these private  universities  and indeed this is of course true so  when i studied here at university of  munich  i almost paid no student fees at all  essentially studying at a public  university in germany  is for free so this is of course  different  to the private universities when i  completed my master in accounting and  finance in london  i paid over 20 000 pounds british pound  in student fees  and i recently checked again the web  page today it costs even over 30  000 pounds this is of course a crazy  amount and can be very  detrimental for other people trying to  study in this way  so how can you do this what can you do  to finance this  and indeed there are lots of  opportunities for scholarships  i would encourage you really to check  out scholarships that might be available  to you  i was privileged enough to pay at least  a significant portion of the total  student fees  with scholarship programs of course the  exact programs that are available to you  depend  on your country on the university on  your region so do this research  though my opinion also is if you really  want to do it if you have a dream  university where you want to study  there are ways to make it work i would  very likely  not not study at such a university only  due to the student fees there are often  ways to finance it  and indeed after you study at such  university especially if you study  something in the area of business  you will often have opportunities to  then also recoup remake the money  rather correctly after graduating at  least if you then also have the goal  to move into one of these high-paced  careers that then provide you with the  salaries that would also enable you  to pay back the student loans that you  might potentially take to finance this  the other question that of course people  have in mind when talking about  public versus private university is the  whole discussion of  target schools is the whole discussion  of whether or not  it really helps your career to study at  these  private schools potentially because they  are considered  a target school which is a school that  is a preferred university  for employers to hire from and indeed  now reflecting on my experience here i  think the first  insight is that you always need to  distinguish local target schools  from global target schools because the  university of munich  even though it is a public university  could be considered  a target school in germany right so this  university has the reputation  in germany that it is one of the leading  business schools and indeed all these  employers that we so frequently talk  about on this channel  like the mbb consulting firms mckinsey  bcg bane and so on  they do like to hire people from the  university of munich  and indeed i was hired for an internship  at mckinsey  when i was studying in the middle of my  bachelor here though the truth is also  probably if you go beyond germany if you  go beyond the country  very few people will really know the  university of munich so it is  a local target school and now you can  compare this to a school like the london  school of economics in the uk  in england this is of course university  which is probably well known  also far outside of the uk many people  in many other countries will know this  university so this is university  that might be considered an  international target school  and if you want this type of reputation  if you want to study at university  with a reputation that exceeds the  boundaries of your region of your  country  it might be worthwhile to go there as  well and yes of course in terms of  target schools  in terms of later potentially also  applying to an mba  or to other larger global firms this  might be helpful  though i would argue most of your career  ambitions  can very much be fulfilled with studying  at a  public university which is a local  target school as well  so i hope that these different  considerations these different  dimensions that i looked at are helpful  to you  if you are in the position to not ask  yourself whether you'd like to study at  a public or private university  but what is my personal conclusion what  is my reflection  on this question and personally i would  not have wanted to miss my time in  munich it was for me an extremely  remarkable  informative time indeed just also from  the cost perspective  given that the undergraduate degree  usually goes three to four years  now the need of having to pay student  fees for all this time  this is of course insane and it's  arguably whether you will  recoup this financial burden than later  in your job  though what i think could be the sweet  spot is to indeed do the undergraduate  degree  at a public university benefit from the  lower cost  from this very remarkable experience  that you get there  and then get for the private university  the master degree because the master  often is only one to two years  so the cost will be lower there you can  then get also all these benefits  without incurring all the cost this is  in the end how i did it and reflecting  on this it did make a lot of sense  for my personal career and also looking  back at some of my peers  many people followed a similar route and  it worked out quite well for them as far  as i can take  so now i'd love to hear from you what  are your experiences did you study at  the public  or private university if you studied at  a private university  what are your reflections was it really  worth your money i'd love to hear from  you  and indeed as you know every comment  that you leave below the video also  helps me with the algorithm  and indeed if you took any value out of  this video at all  please hit the like button for the  youtube algorithm  and also subscribe to my channel to stay  up to date on all my content i release  new videos  every single saturday and if you want to  see even more from me also follow me on  my instagram  my handle is firm learning i now want to  say thanks to all the members of the  channel  you're really making a great  contribution to the course of this  channel  thank you so much and to all the others  of you good weekend to you  hope you are having great days see you  back next saturday this is heine from  from learning  bye

